Description: @DISTRIBUTION@ installer-side data files
 Static data files needed by the Debian Installer ramdisk to run
 against a @DISTRIBUTION@ ISO: stub debconf templates that upstream
 udebs we don't ship would otherwise provide, release-identity
 files (/etc/lsb-release, /etc/default-release), the debootstrap
 suite script for @CODENAME@, the debconf string-override file
 plus startup hook that rebrands installer-visible strings to
 @DISTRIBUTION@.
 .
 Built from local source under fork/source/ and ships only static
 files — no compiled code.  Per docs/branding-methodology.md, no
 upstream installer source is patched for branding; everything
 ships here.
